<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">testāmentārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to wills</i>, <i>testamentary.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(lex) Cornelia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 1, 42, § 108</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adoptio,</span>”
				<i>by will</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 2, 2, § 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hereditates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 50, 16, 130</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">testā-mentārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Ingen., <i>one who draws up a will</i>: si testamentarius contra
			voluntatem testatoris condicionem detraxit. <i><span class="en">Dig. 28, 5,
				9</span></i>, §§ 3 and 6; 29, 6, 1; 36, 1, 3 <i>fin.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In a bad sense, <i>one who forges a
				will</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Sest. 17, 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Off.
				3, 18, 73</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
